  "text": "[LDET.3.6.1] **One rounding mode, the engine's.** Every `Float` operation the\nengine performs is IEEE 754 binary64 arithmetic rounding to nearest, ties to\neven, with subnormals kept and no two operations fused into one. `math.fma` is one\noperation, IEEE 754's fused multiply-add, and not a fusion of two\n([LEXP.3.2.2]). The rounding\nmode is state the host process shares, so the engine must establish\nround-to-nearest-even for its own evaluation whatever mode the integrator's\nthread holds, and must restore the integrator's mode before control passes back\nto the integrator, by a callback or by the return of an engine call. The\nintegrator's own floating-point code never sees the engine's mode.\n\nThe mode the engine restores when an engine call returns is the one the\nintegrator held when it made that call. A mode integrator code sets inside a\ncallback belongs to that callback, and the engine does not keep it.\n\n",
  "refs": [
    "LEXP.3.2.2"
  ],
